# Cloudflare credentials for the scripts in this directory.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (which is gitignored) and fill in the real values.
# The pinned `wrangler deploy` in deploy_web.sh and publish_modules.sh, and the
# `wrangler` and `curl` calls in r2_remove_old_domain.sh / r2_stage2_redirect.sh,
# read these from the environment. The scripts never echo the token and never
# enable `set -x`, so the secret stays out of logs.

# API token minted once by hand in the Cloudflare dashboard
# (My Profile is NOT enough -- create an *Account* API token). Scope it to the
# account and BOTH zones -- umasagashi.com and umacapture.com -- with these
# permissions:
#   - Account > Workers Scripts > Edit       (deploy_web.sh and publish_modules.sh: upload the
#                                             Workers umacapture-web and umacapture-data with
#                                             their assets, put umacapture-web's secret)
#   - Zone    > Workers Routes > Edit        (attach their custom domains, umacapture.com and
#                                             data.umacapture.com)
#   - Account > D1 > Edit                    (the record-sharing databases of production and
#                                             staging: create them, apply migrations)
# r2_remove_old_domain.sh and r2_stage2_redirect.sh additionally need:
#   - Account > Workers R2 Storage > Edit   (list and detach the bucket's custom domains)
#   - Zone    > DNS > Edit                  (the DNS record of a bucket custom domain)
#   - Zone    > Single Redirect > Edit       (stage 2 redirect rule)
#   - Zone    > Zone > Read                  (resolve the zone id)
# data.umacapture.com lives on the umacapture.com zone; the stage 2 redirect rule
# is installed on the umasagashi.com zone (where the legacy hardcoded URLs live).
# The token needs both zones in its scope.
# The release checks in docs/web-deploy.md read, and never change, these:
#   - Account > Turnstile > Read             (the publish widget's hostname and mode)
#   - Zone    > Zone WAF > Read              (the rate-limiting rule in front of /r/ and /api/)
#   - Account > Billing > Read               (the Workers plan)
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# Cloudflare account ID that owns the R2 bucket and both zones
# (umasagashi.com + umacapture.com).
# Dashboard > R2 (or any zone) overview > "Account ID" in the right sidebar.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
